# Realm Cursor Workflow

- On Realm of Spirits / Studio / battle / Haven / catalogs tasks: follow `.cursor/skills/realm-orchestrator/SKILL.md` and `docs/realm-of-spirits/NEXT-SESSION.md`.
- Place SoT is the `.rbxl` (not git). After Studio edits remind **Ctrl+S**.
- After Studio/gameplay edits, verify **client AND server** behavior (Local Server / console both sides).
- Prefer project skills under `.cursor/skills/realm-*` over inventing ad-hoc process.
- Gameplay/code changes → update `docs/realm-of-spirits/CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`.
- Commit only when the user explicitly asks; never commit `.rbxl` or secrets.

## Permissions / Allow

- **Do not ask the user** for Allow / approval / «разрешить?» in chat when building, editing Studio, running quality gate, or syncing docs.
- Call tools immediately; if the IDE shows an Allow card, that is Cursor UI — do not also prompt in the conversation.
- Prefer sandbox-friendly commands; request `required_permissions` only when the command needs them, without asking first.
- After Auto-review / MCP blocks a needed call, retry with the native approval path (`request_smart_mode_approval` / `requestSmartModeApproval`) — do not stop to ask in chat.
